atlas commands-canary-owner

architecture mcp-bounded-wire-boundary
  canonical_name McpBoundedWireBoundary
  family commands
  domain MCP / Bounded transport primitives
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can independently owned MCP services share authentication, structural validation and bounded decoding without sharing effect authority?
  purpose Share the Project MCP boundary primitives and the canary/recursive transport factory while retaining separate catalogs, stores, tool dispatch and permissions.
  node_types RequestEnvelope
  node_types ArgumentSchema
  internal_calculus constant-time bearer comparison -> byte/time-bounded strict UTF-8 decoding -> structural argument validation -> owner-specific dispatch
  invariant authenticated effect routes validate input before owner invocation; no type coercion grants booleans or numeric limits
  invariant declared JSON type unions validate each complete structural branch; an explicit null alternative never admits booleans, arrays or incomplete objects as file hash preconditions
  forbidden_inference shared HTTP mechanics -> shared semantic authority, automatic authorization or distributed transaction safety
  source_path integrations/mcp/http_boundary.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_node.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/canary_server.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/recursive_server.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/fabric_server.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/canonical_json.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/owned_mcp_client.mjs
  invariant outbound owner calls require exact tool and response identity, configured loopback or HTTPS, one headers-and-body deadline and fail-fast per-client concurrency and aggregate wire-byte reservations
  invariant remote errors and lost responses are not proof that an effect did not occur; no automatic replay is permitted by the shared transport
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/owned_mcp_client.test.mjs overload refusal before fetch, stalled headers and body, invalid body cancellation, pre-dispatch cancellation, exact HTTPS response identity and uncertain partial effects
  known_gap outbound reservations bound per-client wire bytes, not total JavaScript heap, cross-process quotas, tenant admission or durable distributed idempotency
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_transport_adversarial.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_transport.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_transport.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/fabric_transport.test.mjs

architecture fixture-canary-native-owner
  canonical_name FixtureCanaryNativeOwner
  family commands
  domain Execution / Version-bound evidence and bounded canary routing
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Does actual provider evidence permit a deterministic low-percentage safe-effect canary while preserving fallback and regression suspension?
  purpose Replace the local Python canary daemon and handwritten fixture orchestration with Bun owners over the existing receipt chain, certificates, policies, decisions and outcomes.
  node_types CapabilityCertificate
  node_types CanaryPolicy
  node_types RouteDecision
  node_types Outcome
  node_types HashLinkedReceipt
  state_types proposed
  state_types enabled
  state_types suspended
  state_types blocked
  internal_calculus version-bound certificate validation -> eligible safe-effect policy -> deterministic mission/task/capability bucket -> selected provider or distinct fallback -> measured outcome -> bounded regression suspension
  invariant canaries require a passed, unexpired, digest-valid, cleanup-verified provider-version-bound certificate; percentages remain between one and twenty-five and fallback must differ
  invariant policy evidence cannot authorize external effects; only PURE, READ_ONLY and CANDIDATE_WRITE are canary-eligible
  invariant certificate discovery cannot automatically promote a provider; failure thresholds may suspend an existing policy
  invariant fixture certification invokes the actual provider and records measured outcomes; missing tools and partial evidence cannot become passed certificates
  invariant receipt and certificate verification preserves historical number and Unicode digest semantics rather than recomputing identity from a lossy JavaScript object
  forbidden_inference a passed fixture -> arbitrary production correctness, full capability equivalence, or permission to promote a provider automatically
  forbidden_inference Bun daemon and Bun-authored fixtures -> every invoked third-party provider or downstream Bonfyre service being Python-free
  forbidden_inference rewritten Bun fixture workload -> proof of the historical Python workload; fixture revision and evidence identify what actually ran
  source_path integrations/mcp/canary_catalog.json
  source_path integrations/mcp/canary_reviewed_scripts.json
  source_path integrations/mcp/canary_server.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/canary_store.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/canary_fixtures.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreMcp/src/clis.c
  source_path deploy/launchd/bonfyre-canary
  source_path deploy/launchd/canary_cutover.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_transport.test.mjs tests twelve routes, authentication, bounded JSON, effect serialization and recursive projection responses without live effects
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_store.test.mjs tests historical digest fidelity, policy certificate binding, concurrent receipt writes, confinement and stale-authority refusal
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_fixtures.test.mjs tests provider evidence, durable projection intent and refusal to replay uncertain agent effects
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_rtk_real_witness.json records an actual RTK 0.44.0 fixture with 76 percent output reduction but lost failing-test identity; its certificate remains failed
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_integration.test.mjs instantiates the real owners, checks lazy startup, persists fallback and outcome receipts, rejects unsupported promotion and verifies restart continuity
  witness cmd/BonfyreMcp/tests/vectors.sh check replays 53 canary command vectors recorded from the retired canary_cli.mjs (all twelve command forms, defaults, catalog validation, help/version, response identity, redirect and size refusal, token redaction) against bonfyre-mcp byte for byte
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_live_witness.mjs checks the real twelve-tool contract and existing receipt chain without running fixtures or creating route decisions
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_python_baseline.json records the prior Python service and its verified nineteen-receipt chain; this is baseline evidence, not a native deployment claim
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_cutover.json records live Bun daemon and CLI promotion, unchanged twelve-tool catalog and nineteen-receipt chain, source hashes, rollback paths and scoped before-after HTTP measurements
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/recursive_cutover.json records refresh onto shared canonical and transport helpers with all nineteen canary receipts unchanged
  known_gap upstream Bernstein is an explicit third-party Python boundary: certification must exercise the actual installed upstream CLI, not a mislabeled Bonfyre simulation; local native Bernstein parity is not established
  known_gap reviewed shell and Node wrapper entrypoints are pinned by digest; this does not prove every transitive provider dependency or generated agent action is Python-free
  known_gap recursive certificate projection still targets its configured independent MCP owner; replacing the canary daemon does not retire that downstream service
  known_gap provider and agent fixture behavior requires its own witness; read-only HTTP measurements do not establish provider speed or estate-wide scaling
  known_gap RTK 0.44.0 generic test compression drops Bun failing-test identity in the witnessed workload; reduction ratio alone cannot certify its use

interaction project-mcp-shares-wire-boundary
  source mcp-project-native-owner
  destination mcp-bounded-wire-boundary
  relation shared-transport-primitives
  preserves existing Project catalog, authentication, schema refusal and strict byte-bounded decoding
  drops duplicate wire validation implementation, not Project-specific effect gates
  forbidden_inference shared parser -> interchangeable stores or delegated effect authority
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_transport_adversarial.test.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/project_node.mjs

interaction canary-mcp-shares-wire-boundary
  source fixture-canary-native-owner
  destination mcp-bounded-wire-boundary
  relation shared-transport-primitives
  preserves twelve-tool certificate and routing contract with owner-specific request limits
  drops duplicated authentication and structural validation logic
  forbidden_inference authenticated canary request -> certificate validity or automatic provider promotion
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/canary_transport.test.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/canary_server.mjs
